.SH "نام (NAME)"
timew-start \- start time tracking
.SH "خلاصه دستور (SYNOPSIS)"
.sp
.nf
\fBtimew start\fP [\fI<date>\fP] [\fI<tag>\fP\fB...\fP]
.fi
.br
.SH "توضیحات (DESCRIPTION)"
.sp
Begins tracking using the current time with any specified set of tags.
If a tag contains multiple words, therefore containing spaces, use quotes to surround the whole tag.
.SH "HINTS"
.sp
The start command accepts the following hints:
.sp
\fB:fill\fP
.RS 4
The \*(Aq:fill\*(Aq hint can be used to create a new interval that starts right after the last closed interval.
This is useful when you want to start tracking time immediately after finishing a previous task without specifying a start time.
.RE
.SH "مثال‌ها (EXAMPLES)"
.sp
For example, this command specifies two tags (\*(Aqweekend\*(Aq and \*(AqHome & Garden\*(Aq), the second of which requires quotes.
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
$ timew start weekend \*(AqHome & Garden\*(Aq
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
An optional date may be specified to indicate the intended start of the tracked time:
.sp
.if n .RS 4
.nf
.fam C
$ timew start 8am weekend \*(AqHome & Garden\*(Aq
.fam
.fi
.if n .RE
.sp
If there is a previous open interval, it will be closed at the given start time.
.sp
Quotes are harmless if used unnecessarily.
.SH "همچنین ببینید (SEE ALSO)"
.sp
\fBtimew\-cancel\fP(1),
\fBtimew\-continue\fP(1),
\fBtimew\-stop\fP(1),
\fBtimew\-track\fP(1)